# Sling git identity

Repos: sling-studio, sling-api, sling-ai, slingEarly, publishloud.

Global git stays TimeDoctor. Set LOCAL `user.email` / `user.name` only. Never `git config --global`.

## Commits

Before every commit, local email MUST be `ankur@sling.biz` and name `Ankur Pata`. Set LOCAL if missing.

```
# BAD — global rewrite, or commit as TimeDoctor
git config --global user.email "ankur@sling.biz"
git commit   # local email is ankur.patankar@timedoctor.com

# GOOD
git config --local user.email "ankur@sling.biz"
git config --local user.name "Ankur Pata"
git commit
```

## GitHub (`gh pr create|merge|close`)

`gh api user` login must be `slingbiz` (or the GitHub user that owns the slingbiz org), NOT `ankurtd`.

If gh is `ankurtd`, do not create/merge/close PRs with gh. Ship with:
`git push git@github-secondary:slingbiz/<repo>.git HEAD:master`
(use `HEAD:main` for sling-ai). Tell Ankur the GitHub PR still shows ankurtd until he uses slingbiz on github.com.

```
# BAD — gh is ankurtd (including "already on master so just gh merge")
gh pr merge 35 --repo slingbiz/sling-studio

# GOOD — gh is slingbiz, or push via github-secondary
gh pr merge 35 --repo slingbiz/sling-studio
git push git@github-secondary:slingbiz/sling-studio.git HEAD:master
```

Exception only if Ankur says it is fine THIS time AND names the PR. The hook still denies ankurtd `gh pr`; he can approve the prompt or run it himself.

Do not rewrite published master history to fix old ankurtd commits.
